comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T17:06:50.343Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-30: canonical GH-1159 owner confirmed after complete all-status duplicate search. Deliver one bounded SDK-owned workspace position read across CLI and MCP, make health --strict-exit require configured merge drivers while preserving advisory default health, and verify clean/prepared/unprepared/pending-receipt/drift states."
  "2026-08-30T19:54:48.388Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-08-30: implemented the public workspacePosition governance SDK and CLI/MCP/runtime contracts; strict health now fails missing clone-local drivers while advisory health remains compatible. PM-linked suite passed 4 files/16 tests. Full repository coverage passed 590/590 files and 8160/8160 tests at exactly 100% statements (60340/60340), branches (45511/45511), functions (12551/12551), and lines (58096/58096). pnpm quality:static passed including ESLint, zero duplication, architecture limits, contracts, refusal closure, token budgets, graph/record integrity, and 100% source/export/member docstrings. Trivy found 0 high/critical findings; npm audit found 0 known vulnerabilities; credential scan and ShellCheck passed. Package artifact gate (1551 files), package-first 88-command dogfood, packed npx/bunx smoke, and independent temporary-directory npm/npx and Bun/bunx SDK/CLI acceptance passed. Real checkout position is ready with configured fence, zero receipts, and zero history drift across 2608 items."
  "2026-08-30T21:00:58.376Z","harness:codex","PR review correction evidence: accepted Greptile's workspace-target finding. Every non-ready next action now embeds an explicitly shell-quoted --pm-path for the exact inspected tracker, so inherited source-write coordinates cannot redirect recovery. A two-repository temporary acceptance enabled PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT, PM_SOURCE_PM_PATH, read-only source context, and the write override; the reported command installed drivers only in the inspected repository, left the source repository untouched, and returned ready. The required token-surface baseline now includes workspace position at 136 bytes and all 55 surfaces pass."
  "2026-08-30T21:02:06.165Z","harness:codex","Final correction gates: PM-linked workspace suite passes 4 files/17 tests; exact repository coverage passes 590 files and 8161 tests at 100/100/100/100; pnpm quality:static passes all source/export/member docstrings, ESLint, zero duplication, contracts, SDK parity, refusal/token/graph/record gates; npm audit, credential scan, Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL, and ShellCheck are clean."
  "2026-08-30T21:18:59.963Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review finding accepted: recovery rendering reused a POSIX-only quoting expression. The correction now delegates tokenized arguments to the public cross-platform renderPmCommand SDK primitive and adds explicit Windows plus POSIX path regression proof."
  "2026-08-30T21:35:59.506Z","harness:codex","Windows portability correction verified: the one next action now delegates tokenized argv to the public renderPmCommand SDK primitive. Explicit Linux and win32 regression cases pass; manual acceptance executed the emitted command for /tmp/.../portable & review's workspace, transitioned merge_fence_unprepared to ready, and removed the sandbox. Exact coverage remains 590 files/8161 tests and 100/100/100/100. quality:static, 55 token surfaces, credential scan, pnpm audit, Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL, tracked ShellCheck, 1551-file package artifact, 88-command package dogfood, and 13-package npx/bunx packed smoke all pass."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T19:54:47.847Z","harness:codex",A workspace readiness primitive is most useful when it composes recorded subsystem state into one deterministic next action; exposing the same public SDK result through CLI and MCP prevents adapters from reimplementing sequencing policy.
  "2026-08-30T21:35:59.968Z","harness:codex",Recovery guidance should be built from tokenized argv through the shared platform-aware command renderer; ad hoc shell quoting cannot satisfy a universal SDK contract across POSIX and Windows.
